Fetch the OpenID Connect metadata only when an SSO token may need it.

Reason: every command that needs a token first fetched
https://accounts.fastly.com/realms/fastly/.well-known/openid-configuration
(configureAuth), and failed when that request failed, although the auth
server it configures is only used to refresh or create an SSO token. With
FASTLY_API_TOKEN, --token or a stored API token, a command now makes no
request before its own, so it costs one round trip through slicc's network
less, and an unreachable accounts endpoint no longer breaks API calls. A
stored SSO token, or FASTLY_USE_SSO=1 without a token, still fetches it.

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: upstream configures the auth server lazily.

diff --git a/pkg/app/run.go b/pkg/app/run.go
--- a/pkg/app/run.go
